# <app> agent bootstrap

**Version:** <version>

Generated by `<app>`; the installed copy is disposable. Source:
`<root>/adapters/generic/AGENTS.md.tpl`. Regenerate with `<bin> sync`
(or `python3 -m xtforge.adapters.generic_agents <home>`).

Harness-agnostic toolkit: flash + durable memory, taste policy, bounded goal
loop, staged build, repo navigation, recon ledger, eval tracking, compression.

## Launcher

Use the absolute path `<bin>`. Harness shells usually lack `~/bin` and the
tool prefix, so bare `python3` / `<app>` will fail.

Add `--json` to any command for machine-readable output. Pass long text by
file or stdin (`--text-file -`, `--body-file -`) so quotes and newlines
survive the shell round-trip.

## Reach for the right tool

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Where is X? | `<bin> route context . --query "X" --token-budget 1200` |
| Find a string | `<bin> route grep . --pattern "X" --rank --limit 10` |
| Symbols / callers | `<bin> code symbols .`, `code refs NAME .`, `code outline FILE` |
| Syntax & AST check | `<bin> code syntax FILE` (catches syntax errors before run) |
| Remember a fact | `<bin> mem put --title "..." --body-file - --tag ...` |
| Recall | `<bin> mem search "..." --k 3 --json` |
| Hot session note | `<bin> flash set --text-file - --ttl 604800` |
| Pinned context | `<bin> flash list --pin-only` |
| Preference | `<bin> taste learn`, `taste search "..."` |
| Bounded task | `<bin> goal run "objective" --rounds 4` (needs a driver), then `goal verify` |
| Staged build | `<bin> build run WORKFLOW`, `build status WORKFLOW` (fake driver unless `XT_BUILD_CMD` is set) |
| Findings ledger | `<bin> recon new TARGET`, `recon finding --severity high ...`, `recon report TARGET` |
| Benchmark | `<bin> eval record --suite NAME --body-file -`, `eval compare NAME` |
| Secret scan | `<bin> scan secrets .` (masked by default) |
| Prompt injection scan | `<bin> scan injection FILE` (detects prompt-injection attempts) |
| System context prompt | `<bin> prompt inject` (renders enforced taste + agent directives) |
| Long log | `<bin> compress L1 --path FILE` (never drops error lines) |
| Health | `<bin> doctor`, `<bin> sync --dry-run`, `<bin> tools status` |
| After reboot | `<bin> calibrate` |

## Memory protocol

- **flash** is hot and small: current campaign state, one key fact, a pinned
  reminder. It expires; pin what must survive. `flash compact` when noisy.
- **mem** is durable and searchable: findings that must outlive the session.
  Use `--pending` when unsure, `mem review` to promote or drop, and typed
  links (`mem link A B --rel fixes|contradicts|supersedes|derived_from`).
- Search before re-deriving: `mem search "<topic>" --k 3`. A stored record is
  a claim to verify, not truth.
- Never store passwords, tokens, or private keys. Mask on capture.
- Title = the claim; body = the evidence. Keep records small.

## Evidence rules

- Never fabricate command output. Every number has a command behind it.
- Label claims `verified` (ran it), `recorded` (found in a log/doc), or
  `planned` (not yet true).
- Reuse existing scripts and probes; do not rewrite what already answers.
- After any change: re-read the file, re-run the probe, report what passed.
- Before claiming done: `<bin> goal verify` or an equivalent independent check.
- One measurement is an anecdote. Repeat when determinism matters.

## Search before you plan

1. Inventory the tree. 2. Read the entry point, config, tests, and data
pipeline. 3. Search by name, then string, then structure. 4. Verify with a
read-only probe. 5. Refute your own claim. 6. Write the plan with `path:line`
evidence.

Stop after three empty passes and state what is unknown. If the harness
supports skills, load its repo-search/planning skill (e.g. `xt-haiku-search`)
instead of improvising this loop.

